        "rendered_context": "[S1]\nPreceding paragraph:\nBaggage allowance details shown are indications for Kenya Airways-operated flights only and may be subject to change depending on the aircraft operated on the day of travel. Flights operated by other airlines under a Kenya Airways flight number may be subject to other baggage restrictions.\n\nTable (Body/block 6):\n\nOpening row (context, not a declared header):\nRow 1: Column 1: ROUTING (<-> FROM/TO) | Column 2: BUSINESS CLASS | Column 3: ECONOMY\nRow 2: Column 1: Africa <-> America/Europe | Column 2: 2 PC 32kg/70lbs max each | Column 3: 2 PC 23kg/50lbs max each\nRow 3: Column 1: Africa <-> Middle East /Asia\n \n (incl Bangkok-Guangzhou) | Column 2: 2 PC 32kg/70lbs max each | Column 3: 2 PC 23kg/50lbs max each\nRow 4: Column 1: Bangkok <-> Guangzhou-Bangkok | Column 2: 1 PC 32kg/70lbs max each | Column 3: 1 PC 23kg/50lbs max each\nRow 5: Column 1: Nairobi <-> Mumbai | Column 2: 1 PC 32kg/70lbs max each | Column 3: 1 PC 23kg/50lbs max each\nRow 6: Column 1: Africa <-> Africa | Column 2: 2 PC 32kg/70lbs max each | Column 3: 2 PC 23kg/50lbs max each\nRow 7: Column 1: Domestic | Column 2: 1 PC 32kg/70lbs max each | Column 3: 1 PC 23kg/50lbs max each\n\nFollowing paragraph:\nFREQUENT FLYER MEMBERS\n\n[S1]\nPreceding paragraph:\nReference Table\n\nTable (Body/block 11):\n\nOpening row (context, not a declared header):\nRow 1: Column 1: Domestic | Column 2: Kisumu, Mombasa, and Malindi\nRow 2: Column 1: Africa | Column 2: All Africa points\nRow 3: Column 1: Middle East/Asia | Column 2: Middle East and Asian points\nRow 4: Column 1: Europe/America | Column 2: All Europe and American points\nRow 5: Column 1: 5th freedom Sectors | Column 2: Flights that carry passengers to and from any point without connecting through the hub (Nairobi), e.g., Accra to Monrovia, Abidjan to Dakar\n\nFollowing paragraph:\n[List level 1] - As a mandatory standard each piece of checked in baggage shall have a name label that bears the passenger's name, physical address, and phone number on the outside and also on the inside. The name should be the same as the one mentioned on the ticket. An email address is also recommended.\n\n[S1]\nBaggage Allowance\n\nLink to Baggage Allowance website page: https://www.kenya-airways.com/en-ke/plan/baggage-information/baggage-allowance/\n\nFree Checked Baggage Allowance:\n\nBaggage allowance details shown are indications for Kenya Airways-operated flights only and may be subject to change depending on the aircraft operated on the day of travel. Flights operated by other airlines under a Kenya Airways flight number may be subject to other baggage restrictions.",
