      "shared_pipeline": {
        "retrieval_ms": 364.966,
        "context_build_ms": 2.483,
        "retrieved_chunks": [
          {
            "rank": 1,
            "parent_chunk_id": "65bd106b254593394ebf37ebaca07b41c54d771546bcba340c46f0cca1a17a63",
            "document": "Special Care.docx",
            "section": null,
            "text": "– Wheelchair Assistance:\n\n[List level 1] - Passengers traveling to or from London Heathrow (LHR), London Gatwick (LGW), and Paris Charles de Gaulle (CDG) are kindly advised to request wheelchair assistance at least 48 hours before departure.\n\n[List level 1] - Requests submitted within 48 hours of departure cannot be guaranteed, and service availability will be subject to operational constraints at the airport.\n\nWhat Type of Wheelchair can you Bring?\n\n[List level 1] - You may bring your own wheelchair or other mobility aid or assistive devices free of charge and make your reservation at least 48 hours before departure.\n\n[List level 1] - If you have a manual wheelchair that is collapsible or dismountable, you can bring it as hand baggage as long as it doesn’t exceed the maximum dimensions as below:",
            "score": 0.8861834461109721
          },
          {
            "rank": 2,
            "parent_chunk_id": "8e5cf792a3dc59e0cc270af0b4b3b24d3ebeb639c75e89630ab571f6cb242e1a",
            "document": "Special Care.docx",
            "section": null,
            "text": "committed to making your journey with your infant as smooth and comfortable as possible. We value your trust in us and look forward to serving you and your family on board.\n\nReduced Mobility\n\nPassengers with Reduced Mobility\n\nGeneral Information\n\n[List level 1] - Passengers with reduced mobility are those with a medical or neurodevelopmental disabilities who require individual attention, not given to passengers normally during (dis)embarkation, during the flight, during ground handling and/or in case of an emergency evacuation.\n\n[List level 1] - Wheelchair services shall be provided to passengers free of charge. Kindly contact us through our 24-hour contact center on Tel: +254 734 104 747, Mobile: +254 711 024 747, WhatsApp: +254 705 474 747, or talk to us through 'Our Feedback Form '. We will look into the possibilities and make a reservation for you right away.\n\n[List level 1] - Familiarize yourself with your legal rights. For flights into and out of the USA, the airline passengers with disabilities bill of rights guarantees the fundamental rights of air travelers with disabilities.\n\n[List level 1] - Important Notice for London Heathrow (LHR), London Gatwick(LGW), and Paris Charles de Gaulle Flights(CDG) – Wheelchair Assistance:\n\n[List level 1] - Passengers traveling to or from London Heathrow (LHR), London Gatwick (LGW), and Paris Charles de Gaulle (CDG) are kindly advised to request wheelchair assistance at least 48 hours before departure.",
            "score": 0.8674739597951275
          },
          {
            "rank": 3,
            "parent_chunk_id": "b8a7375af85062c4a6c9ac1553dff197fb26900b689c856517bcc3228f183fd7",
            "document": "Check-in.docx",
            "section": null,
            "text": "identification during check-in. It is required to complete the check-in process at least one and a half hours prior to departure, regardless of the travel class. The check-in counters close half an hour before takeoff.\n\nCheck-in from China Guangzhou:\n\nPassengers departing from China Guangzhou are advised to note that the check-in counters in this location will be closed an hour and a half (90 minutes) before the scheduled flight departure.\n\nPriority Check-in:\n\nTravelers who hold Asante Rewards Elite status (Gold and Platinum levels) and are flying from Nairobi to any destination can enjoy the privileges of priority check-in and boarding. This also includes access to the lounge with one guest. Always remember to present your Asante Rewards card at the counter to automatically register your earned miles. If you possess sufficient miles, request an upgrade to experience the services of our business class.",
            "score": 0.8251987470617943
          },
          {
            "rank": 4,
            "parent_chunk_id": "387d08b9fd60495e7a58af6e371cb0f34c0ab5b1763b61ebe8e2bd86bd730b9a",
            "document": "Check-in.docx",
            "section": null,
            "text": "By optig for online check-in, you're not just saving time; you're ensuring a smooth and stress-free start to your journey. Say goodbye to long lines and hello to an effortless way to prepare for your flight\n\nWhen can I Check in?\n\nOnline Check-in:\n\nWith an electronic ticket, online check-in can be performed from 48 hours up until 1 hour before departure. By taking advantage of this service, you can bypass long lines at selected airports and even pick your preferred seat. Once completed, you can print your boarding pass at your convenience. When you arrive at the airport, use the designated online check-in drop-off point for your luggage and then proceed to the boarding gate. Kenya Airways has taken online check-in to new heights, providing a smoother and more convenient experience.\n\nInternational Check-in:\n\nFor international flights, it is mandatory for all passengers to complete the check-in process a minimum of two and a half hours before the flight's departure, regardless of the travel class. The check-in counters close precisely one hour before the scheduled departure time.\n\nDomestic Check-in:\n\nPassengers traveling on domestic flights must present a valid form of identification during check-in. It is required to complete the check-in process at least one and a half hours prior to departure, regardless of the travel class. The check-in counters close half an hour before takeoff.\n\nCheck-in from China Guangzhou:",
            "score": 0.8237236069733853
          },
          {
            "rank": 5,
            "parent_chunk_id": "a0f3e20eb1e4e62312acd729c2fbf42374c4e069242c7ccdb15a46693476e89b",
            "document": "Special Care.docx",
            "section": null,
            "text": "Other types of wheelchairs will be transported as check-in baggage. After checking in, you can use one of the wheelchairs we have available for you at the airport.\n\nPassengers with reduced mobility travelling alone\n\nExcept as provided by applicable law, passengers may travel alone on our flights provided they are self supporting on board and can assist in their own evacuation should the need arise.\n\n[List level 1] - Self-supporting means that:\n\n[List level 1] - Passenger can be able to eat unassisted.\n\n[List level 1] - Passenger can administer his/her medication unassisted.\n\n[List level 1] - If necessary, the passenger can visit the lavatory unassisted. Help from the crew is limited to bringing the onboard wheelchair to the passenger and pushing it to and from the lavatory door. Therefore, the passenger shall be required to lift him/herself -using the upper body power - in and out of the onboard wheelchair unassisted.\n\n[List level 1] - If the passenger is not self-supporting, he/she must travel with a companion(i.e., personal care attendant) who is able to perform these functions; except that for flights to and from the U.S., a safety assistant shall not be required to accompany a passenger except as permitted by applicable law.\n\nPassengers with Reduced Mobility Travelling as a Group\n\n1. Groups of 5 or more passengers shall be handled in a manner conforming with the normal group handling procedures, except that advance arrangements shall be made to provide additional ground equipment and assistance staff necessary, consistent with applicable law.",
            "score": 0.8447095977384708
          }
        ],
