            "parent_chunk_id": "be668733ee527bfd39f2309ad157f816fe59ceced4e8af299db91bd666cf51ea",
            "document": "Payments.docx",
            "section": null,
            "text": "through their own bank.\n\nWhen making a purchase online:\n\n[List level 1] - Select iDEAL as the payment method.\n\n[List level 1] - You’re redirected to your bank’s online banking environment.\n\n[List level 1] - After logging in, confirm the payment.\n\n[List level 1] - The transaction is processed instantly, and once we receive payment confirmation, you will be sent an e-ticket and payment confirmation by e-mail.\n\nOptional Fees\n\nKenya Airways provides a variety of extra services that can be added to your flight with us in accordance with your individual travel requirements. The prices that would be charged upon purchase are listed below along with a list of these optional services.\n\nName Change Fees\n\nKenya Airways will collect service fees for every name change or correction on KQ operated flight bookings and not on an interline basis, using the following applicable fees:-\n\nName Correction",
            "score": 0.8496460690203814
          },
          {
            "rank": 2,
            "parent_chunk_id": "6197c7f0fbba5bdaf1d4d36e56c38e8f7d776e0309e4f41fed1957cec863b5cb",
            "document": "Conditions of Carriage.docx",
            "section": null,
            "text": "The name on the Ticket must exactly match the name in the Passenger’s valid passport or travel document. Travel may be denied if the names do not match.\n\n3.1.2 A Ticket is not transferable, except as required by any locally applicable laws.\n\n3.1.3 Some Tickets are sold at discounted fares which may be partially or completely non-refundable. You should choose the fare best suited to your needs. You may also wish to ensure that you have appropriate insurance to cover instances where you have to cancel your Ticket.\n\n3.1.4 If you have a Ticket, as described in Article 3.1.3, which is completely unused, and you are prevented from travelling due to Force Majeure, provided that you promptly advise us and furnish evidence of such Force Majeure, we will provide you with a credit of the non-refundable amount of the fare, for future travel on us, subject to deduction of a reasonable administration fee. Such credit will remain valid for a minimum of twelve (12) months from the date of issue.\n\n3.1.5 The Ticket is and remains at all times the property of the issuing carrier.\n\n3.1.6 You shall not be entitled to be carried on a flight unless you provide positive identification and a valid Electronic Ticket duly issued in your name.\n\n3.1.7 A ticket is valuable and you should take appropriate measures to safeguard it.\n\n3.2 PERIOD OF VALIDITY",
            "score": 0.8289634500240404
          },
          {
            "rank": 3,
            "parent_chunk_id": "6cf80311fedac48f56d8f27de2b32fe14c463155e50b344defa784d8107c5418",
            "document": "Conditions of Carriage.docx",
            "section": null,
            "text": "or reversing the direction you travel, can result in an increase in price. Many special fares are valid only on the dates and for the flights shown on the Ticket and may not be changed at all, or may be changed only upon payment of an additional fee.\n\n3.3.5 Each Flight Coupon contained in your Ticket will be accepted for carriage in the class of service on the date and flight for which space has been reserved. When a Ticket is originally issued without a reservation being specified, space may be later reserved subject to our Tariff and the availability of space on the flight requested.\n\n3.3.6 Please be advised that in the event you do not show up for any flight without advising us in advance, we may cancel your return or onward reservations. However, if you do advise us in advance, we will not cancel your subsequent flight reservations.\n\n3.4 NAME AND ADDRESS OF CARRIER\n\nOur name may be abbreviated to our Airline Designator Code, or otherwise, in the Ticket. Our address is P O Box 19002, Embakasi, Nairobi, Kenya\n\nARTICLE 4: FARES, TAXES, FEES AND CHARGES\n\n4.1 FARES",
            "score": 0.8163569656271404
          },
          {
            "rank": 4,
            "parent_chunk_id": "e234612580708c736de8b0d31111e099e584b3ae25a67c82efcb9b14b5c4b9de",
            "document": "Special Care.docx",
            "section": null,
            "text": "Get the form here(Link:https://www.kenya-airways.com/globalassets/commercial/plan/special-care/unaccompanied-minors/kq_unaccompaniedminor_form.pdf ).\n\nUnaccompanied Minors are accepted only on Kenya Airways-operated flights.\n\nExpert Support & Fees:\n\n[List level 1] - Expert Assistance: A dedicated team handles the booking process, ensuring all necessary information about the child, parents/guardians, and the designated pick-up person is collected accurately.\n\n[List level 1] - Unaccompanied Minor Fee: While a fee applies for unaccompanied minor services, it covers the personalized care, support, and supervision provided during the trip. The fee is exempted for Domestic travel only, (NBO, MBA, KIS)\n\n[List level 1] - Unaccompanied Minor Groups: If an unaccompanied minor group is not accompanied by an adult, unaccompanied minor fees will apply. If accompanied by an adult, our standard group policy will apply.\n\nNB: We also provide the service to young adults aged 15 to 17 upon request from a parent or guardian.\n\nTailored Flights, Smooth Transitions, and Efficient Check-In:\n\n[List level 1] - Tailored Flights: Our system helps you choose flights that align with your child's schedule, with a focus on non-stop or minimally connected routes for a smoother journey.\n\n[List level 1] - Transition at International Airports: For passengers with separate documents and onward domestic sectors on other airlines, our unaccompanied minor service concludes at the international airport. This ensures a seamless transition.",
            "score": 0.8172204920133517
          },
          {
            "rank": 5,
            "parent_chunk_id": "942b296f5cb1e3fb34ab2b809cb36167d47e721774ea249b612ffea8d6a38c3a",
            "document": "Payments.docx",
            "section": null,
            "text": "money, buy airtime, pay bills, pay for goods and services from their mobile phones. Once the guest opts to make a payment via Tigo pesa, the e-ticket is sent to their email address.\n\nOther Methods of Payment (AMOPs)\n\nMobile Banking or Bank Transfer\n\nThis form of payment is currently available in the Kenya, Nigeria and a few selected African countries. It is a real time 24-hour digital payment solution that allows for bank-to-bank transfers at a low cost. it is easy to use, fast, convenient, secure and affordable. This option is available for online banking, mobile apps, and USSD mobile banking.\n\nCash Payment\n\nYou can pay by cash after you have made your online booking. You then pay and retrieve your ticket at a Kenya Airways ticket office. Important to note: there is usually a fee charged for cash payments. If you wish to pay at the ticket office, make sure to bring along the booking confirmation or booking code that you received by e-mail. Please note: Not all ticket offices accept cash payments.\n\nOnline banking, also known as ‘Real Time Online Banking’ (RTOB), allows you to shop and pay online safely and easily. Payment services include the below:\n\nPayPal\n\nWe accept PayPal as one of the convenient online payment methods. Customers with a PayPal account can make payments on our website and confirm their ticket payment securely. Once the payment confirmation is received, we will issue the electronic ticket to the customer via email.\n\nChina Union Pay",
