      "case_id": "dev-refund-en",
      "semantic_group": "dev-refund",
      "model_id": "openrouter_gemma_26b",
      "language": "en",
      "question": "Can a discounted non-refundable ticket ever receive a credit after force majeure?",
      "fixed_history": null,
      "reference_answer": "Yes. For a completely unused discounted ticket with a non-refundable amount, if force majeure prevents travel, promptly notify KQ and provide evidence. KQ provides credit of the non-refundable fare for future KQ travel, less a reasonable administration fee, valid for at least 12 months from issue. This is credit, not a guaranteed cash refund.",
      "expected_behavior": "answer_with_exception",
      "status": "failed",
      "final_response": null,
      "decision": null,
      "generation_called": true,
      "generation_ms": null,
      "response_time_ms": null,
      "citations": [],
      "sources": [],
      "shared_pipeline": {
        "retrieval_ms": 230.697,
        "context_build_ms": 2.501,
        "retrieved_chunks": [
          {
            "rank": 1,
            "parent_chunk_id": "6197c7f0fbba5bdaf1d4d36e56c38e8f7d776e0309e4f41fed1957cec863b5cb",
            "document": "Conditions of Carriage.docx",
            "section": null,
            "text": "The name on the Ticket must exactly match the name in the Passenger’s valid passport or travel document. Travel may be denied if the names do not match.\n\n3.1.2 A Ticket is not transferable, except as required by any locally applicable laws.\n\n3.1.3 Some Tickets are sold at discounted fares which may be partially or completely non-refundable. You should choose the fare best suited to your needs. You may also wish to ensure that you have appropriate insurance to cover instances where you have to cancel your Ticket.\n\n3.1.4 If you have a Ticket, as described in Article 3.1.3, which is completely unused, and you are prevented from travelling due to Force Majeure, provided that you promptly advise us and furnish evidence of such Force Majeure, we will provide you with a credit of the non-refundable amount of the fare, for future travel on us, subject to deduction of a reasonable administration fee. Such credit will remain valid for a minimum of twelve (12) months from the date of issue.\n\n3.1.5 The Ticket is and remains at all times the property of the issuing carrier.\n\n3.1.6 You shall not be entitled to be carried on a flight unless you provide positive identification and a valid Electronic Ticket duly issued in your name.\n\n3.1.7 A ticket is valuable and you should take appropriate measures to safeguard it.\n\n3.2 PERIOD OF VALIDITY",
            "score": 0.8750943884617263
          },
          {
            "rank": 2,
            "parent_chunk_id": "9c77c900c87aa376cd1859fe44c07825566b47dd9dbc7bd3ec42ad2b2410cba6",
            "document": "Online Refunds.docx",
            "section": null,
            "text": "Ticket and Will Not be Traveling. Can I Obtain a Refund?:\n\n[List level 1] - You have one year from the ticket's original issue date to reschedule your travel without losing the full value of the ticket (less any applicable change fees).\n\n[List level 1] - In addition should the Passenger not travel on a flight and they are holding a refundable or a non refundable ticket they are equally to benefit from a refund of said applicable taxes, charges and other fees.",
            "score": 0.8425926834798549
          },
          {
            "rank": 3,
            "parent_chunk_id": "b55f3c38dccb95421d5de04490eb03c158be4d3e8928b344ec095238f05ec86f",
            "document": "Conditions of Carriage.docx",
            "section": null,
            "text": "or other value document held in our database.   \"ELECTRONIC TICKET\" means the Itinerary/Receipt issued by us or on our behalf, the Electronic Coupons and, if applicable, a boarding document, and shall have the same legal validity as a paper Ticket.\n\n\"FLIGHT COUPON\" means that portion of the Ticket that bears the notation \"good for passage,\" or in the case of an Electronic Ticket, the Electronic Coupon, and indicates the particular places between which you are entitled to be carried.\n\n\"FLIGHT DURATION\" means the scheduled time between departure and arrival of a flight as published in our timetable or confirmed at the time of booking.\n\n\"FORCE MAJEURE\" means unusual and unforeseeable circumstances beyond your control, the consequences of which could not have been avoided even if all due care had been exercised, including but not limited to acts of God, natural disasters, strikes, lockouts, civil commotion, acts of terrorism, governmental restrictions, public health emergencies, and air traffic control delays. Force Majeure shall not include events that are reasonably within your control such as failure to hold necessary travel documents or to arrive at the airport on time.\n\n\"ITINERARY/RECEIPT\" means a document or documents issued by us or on our behalf to Passengers travelling on Electronic Tickets that contains the Passenger's name, flight information and notices.",
            "score": 0.8367933059177223
          },
          {
            "rank": 4,
            "parent_chunk_id": "64d5b752d09760edc28abe0d07e6605eca5e501655f50be35393a90a3f6dae2a",
            "document": "Conditions of Carriage.docx",
            "section": null,
            "text": "our Tariff and is for the transportation as shown on the Ticket. It forms an essential part of our contract with you. The Ticket will not be honored and will lose its validity if all the Coupons are not used in the sequence provided in the Ticket.\n\n3.3.2 Should you wish to change any aspect of your transportation you must contact us in advance. The fare for your new transportation will be calculated and you will be given the option of accepting the new price or maintaining your original transportation as ticketed. Should you be required to change any aspect of your transportation due to Force Majeure, you must contact us as soon as practicable and we will use reasonable efforts to transport you to your next Stopover or final destination, without recalculation of the fare.\n\n3.3.3 Should you change your transportation without our agreement, we will assess the correct price for your actual travel. You will have to pay any difference between the price you have paid and the total price applicable for your revised transportation. We will refund you the difference if the new price is lower, but otherwise your unused Coupons have no value.\n\n3.3.4 Please be aware that while some types of changes will not result in a change of fare, others, such as changing the place of departure (for example, if you do not fly the first segment) or reversing the direction you travel, can result in an increase in price. Many special fares are valid only on the dates and for the flights shown on the Ticket and may not be changed at all, or may be changed only upon payment of an additional fee.",
            "score": 0.8458353225421561
          },
          {
            "rank": 5,
            "parent_chunk_id": "cdbce02fc752171a3baa2b309aeeec424e5f1d085ff63730183ff3987eaf9a6c",
            "document": "FAQs.docx",
            "section": null,
            "text": "of payment and will be widely accepted as a receipt.\n\nAfter booking your flight on Kenya-airways.com you will receive your ticket via e-mail as soon as we have received the payment.\n\nCan I pay for a ticket for another person travelling from abroad?\n\nYes, you can book for another person travelling from abroad. However, if you choose to pay with credit or debit cards you may be required to present the card used for booking, it must be presented while checking into your flight at the commencement of travel. If you, as the credit card holder, are not travelling, a copy of the credit card with an authorization signed by yourself should be presented at check-in. alternatively, the card or a copy of the card with your signed authorization can be presented to the nearest Kenya airways ticketing office at least 72 hours before the flight. This verification is required to ensure a smooth check-in process at the airport and to avoid being refused carriage. Failure to comply will result in the requirement to pay the full ticket cost at the airport or refusal of carriage.\n\nIs it possible for one to modify Multicity bookings online?\n\nNo, It is not possible for any changes to be made on multi-city bookings.\n\nCan one make changes online to bookings that have been affected by schedule change?\n\nNo, one has to call our Contact center for Assistance.\n\nWhen one is a no show can they make any changes to their booking online?\n\nNo this is not possible, one has to call our contact center for Assistance.\n\nWhat happens to bookings that have been cancelled?",
            "score": 0.8346335439006978
          }
        ],
        "complete_supplied_evidence": [
          {
            "citation_id": "S1",
            "parent_chunk_id": "6197c7f0fbba5bdaf1d4d36e56c38e8f7d776e0309e4f41fed1957cec863b5cb",
            "text": "The name on the Ticket must exactly match the name in the Passenger’s valid passport or travel document. Travel may be denied if the names do not match.\n\n3.1.2 A Ticket is not transferable, except as required by any locally applicable laws.\n\n3.1.3 Some Tickets are sold at discounted fares which may be partially or completely non-refundable. You should choose the fare best suited to your needs. You may also wish to ensure that you have appropriate insurance to cover instances where you have to cancel your Ticket.\n\n3.1.4 If you have a Ticket, as described in Article 3.1.3, which is completely unused, and you are prevented from travelling due to Force Majeure, provided that you promptly advise us and furnish evidence of such Force Majeure, we will provide you with a credit of the non-refundable amount of the fare, for future travel on us, subject to deduction of a reasonable administration fee. Such credit will remain valid for a minimum of twelve (12) months from the date of issue.\n\n3.1.5 The Ticket is and remains at all times the property of the issuing carrier.\n\n3.1.6 You shall not be entitled to be carried on a flight unless you provide positive identification and a valid Electronic Ticket duly issued in your name.\n\n3.1.7 A ticket is valuable and you should take appropriate measures to safeguard it.\n\n3.2 PERIOD OF VALIDITY",
            "retrieval_rank": 1,
            "score": 0.8750943884617263
          },
