            "document": "Baggage Allowance Information.docx",
            "section": null,
            "text": "Baggage Allowance\n\nLink to Baggage Allowance website page: https://www.kenya-airways.com/en-ke/plan/baggage-information/baggage-allowance/\n\nFree Checked Baggage Allowance:\n\nBaggage allowance details shown are indications for Kenya Airways-operated flights only and may be subject to change depending on the aircraft operated on the day of travel. Flights operated by other airlines under a Kenya Airways flight number may be subject to other baggage restrictions.",
            "score": 0.8631451815509215
          },
          {
            "rank": 2,
            "parent_chunk_id": "aa717413ce00f5e237caad78098ad5240e17c45fbc0979937b381cdda095d2cb",
            "document": "Baggage Allowance Information.docx",
            "section": null,
            "text": "is automatically calculated in compliance with IATA Resolution 302.\n\n[List level 1] - Free baggage allowance applied will be as stated in the Departure Control System (DCS) or on the e-ticket.\n\nInterline and Codeshare Allowance and Sharing Policy\n\nIATA Resolution 302 determines the Most Significant Carrier (MSC) whose baggage allowance is applied when the journey involves Interline partners. Journeys that involve interline partners/codeshare partners apply different baggage allowances:\n\n[List level 1] - The free baggage allowance shown on the ticket, the trip summary or in the check in system for interline or code share flights is granted.\n\n[List level 1] - For flights originating or terminating to the US/CANADA, piece concept applies based on the specified weight.\n\n[List level 1] - Excess baggage charges are applied through to the final destination.\n\nPooling of Allowance\n\n[List level 1] - Pooling of excess bags is allowed for families or a group or party travelling to a common destination e.g. sportsmen, affinity groups etc.\n\n[List level 1] - The families or group or party shall be travelling together and check-in their baggage to the same destination on the same flight(s) at the same time.\n\n[List level 1] - Each individual passenger shall always be given their own individual baggage” claim” tag.\n\n[List level 1] - For security reasons only families are allowed to register their checked baggage in one check-in record.",
            "score": 0.8528704772664193
          },
          {
            "rank": 3,
            "parent_chunk_id": "9fe66089494a750cb2e8b6e5c976e978cfdda6c48dc0d186b98eb7510834ff8d",
            "document": "Flight upgrade.docx",
            "section": null,
            "text": "takes about ten (10) working days to reflect in your account.\n\n15. An Upgrade that has been issued by the Airline cannot be assigned or transferred, in whole or in part to another person or flight except as specified by these Terms and Conditions.\n\n16. In the event that the Airline cancels a flight and re-accommodates you on to another flight, any Offer you made in relation to the original booking may be transferred to the new flight(s) subject always to availability of seats in Business Class. If, for any reason, there are not enough seats available in business class to fulfill your Upgrade (only where the Offer has been accepted and paid for), any amounts paid by you for the Upgrade will be refunded to the credit card that was used to pay for the upgrade.\n\n17. In the event your booking is transferred to a flight operated by another airline, we cannot guarantee an Upgrade to the higher class. In this case any amounts that you paid for the Upgrade will be refunded to the credit card that was used to pay for the Upgrade and the above-mentioned set off rules will apply.\n\n18. If you had purchased a chargeable seat on an Economy ticket and later upgraded to business class on the same leg, the amount paid for the chargeable seat will be refunded.\n\n19. The fare conditions for the original economy ticket that you purchased shall remain in effect and will be applicable even if your Offer has been accepted and you have been upgraded, including, but not limited to, cancellation policies, change fees, and rules relating to the accrual of frequent flyer miles.",
            "score": 0.886399343663994
          },
          {
            "rank": 4,
            "parent_chunk_id": "e59caebaa2e3d4febd4d6409ca9c8c8d2f07a291841d22ea84b0b2fb094b06f9",
            "document": "Baggage Allowance Information.docx",
            "section": null,
            "text": "FREQUENT FLYER MEMBERS\n\n(All Routes) Asante Silver, Gold & Platinum tiers: 1 additional PC as per the cabin of travel i.e 23kgs economy and 32kgs for business class\n\nReference Table",
            "score": 0.8111354767663945
          },
          {
            "rank": 5,
            "parent_chunk_id": "1346c76983fd6d874478f20b3716fdc3829e7d044d90af47e16be8560257885d",
            "document": "FAQs.docx",
            "section": null,
            "text": "has to call our Contact center for Assistance.\n\nWhen one is a no show can they make any changes to their booking online?\n\nNo this is not possible, one has to call our contact center for Assistance.\n\nWhat happens to bookings that have been cancelled?\n\nOne cannot access any bookings that have been cancelled online.\n\nIs it possible for one to modify bookings online that have already been modified offline?\n\nNo,once changes have been made to a booking offline they cannot be modified online.\n\nCan one change a group PNR?\n\nNo, The maximum number of passengers in a booking that can be modified is 9\n\nCan one modify an award ticket online?\n\nNo, Tickets purchased with miles  cannot be modified online\n\nCan one change a booking one hour to flight time?\n\nNo, kindly call the Contact center for Assistance\n\nUpgrade to Business Class FAQs\n\nWhat is Upgrade to Business Class?\n\nKenya Airways offers you the opportunity to determine your own price for your Business Class upgrade by submitting an offer. KQ will inform you 12 hours before departure whether or not your Upgrade has been approved.\n\nOn which routes is Upgrade to Business Class being offered?\n\nKQ offers Upgrades on all scheduled flights in all routes.\n\nWho can make an Offer for an Upgrade?\n\nTo be able to make an offer you need a valid and issued KQ Economy Class ticket for a scheduled flight operated by KQ. You may submit your Smart Upgrade offer up to 14 hours before Departure.\n\nIs every Economy Class passenger eligible for getting a Business Class Upgrade?",
            "score": 0.879907671438168
          }
        ],
