          {
            "rank": 1,
            "parent_chunk_id": "76643c828fc6fb4b87d43f454813fb09c8bea2b26343d64aeed622d8f3e85391",
            "document": "FAQs.docx",
            "section": null,
            "text": "same amount. Otherwise, we will refund the amount.\n\nWhat happens if an Offer was cancelled by mistake?\n\nUp to 13 hours before departure you may cancel, correct your offer or re-offer.\n\nIs the time of making the Offer decisive for its ranking?\n\nNo.\n\nYou are travelling as a couple or family?\n\nUpgrade to business class considers all passengers within a joint booking.\n\nYou are travelling with a colleague who does not want to Upgrade to Business Class?\n\nAs long as you are not registered under one and the same booking number, you may submit your individual offer.\n\nWhat are the benefits of the KQ Upgrade to Business Class?\n\nYou receive an upgrade at an exceptional price and benefit from all amenities of the KQ Business Class, such as:\n\n[List level 1] - Award-winning Business Class Service and delicious catering\n\n[List level 1] - Access to our worldwide Business Lounges** including meals and drinks\n\n[List level 1] - Check-in at the Business Class counter and fast lane service**\n\n[List level 1] - NOTE: Business class passengers do not have miles accrual as a benefit\n\nCan Miles & More members redeem award miles for Upgrades?\n\nNo.\n\nWill the KQ Upgrade to Business Class change the conditions of your ticket?\n\nNo. The same rules apply as the original fare purchased, including Change Fees and Cancellation Penalties.\n\nIs it possible for one to modify Multicity bookings online?\n\nNo, It is not possible for any changes to be made on multi-city bookings.\n\nCan one make changes online to bookings that have been affected by schedule change?\n\nNo, one has to call our Contact center for Assistance.",
            "score": 0.8482578050412911
          },
          {
            "rank": 2,
            "parent_chunk_id": "e59caebaa2e3d4febd4d6409ca9c8c8d2f07a291841d22ea84b0b2fb094b06f9",
            "document": "Baggage Allowance Information.docx",
            "section": null,
            "text": "FREQUENT FLYER MEMBERS\n\n(All Routes) Asante Silver, Gold & Platinum tiers: 1 additional PC as per the cabin of travel i.e 23kgs economy and 32kgs for business class\n\nReference Table",
            "score": 0.8071893731581768
          },
          {
            "rank": 3,
            "parent_chunk_id": "0112dbfe8e254d64f8ee4da022d1775c1c855fa2884cefbbdd9422dac8a3cd4c",
            "document": "Flight upgrade.docx",
            "section": null,
            "text": "onboard with a wide array of fine wines.\n\n[List level 1] - More than 100 movies, documentaries, and radio shows on a 15 inch screen for your in-flight entertainment.\n\n[List level 1] - A wide selection of newspapers and international magazines.\n\nNOTE: Tickets upgraded to Business class on the basis of a last minute airport upgrade, bid-upgrade, QR Code or on a complimentary basis accrue points on the basis of the original ticket purchased.\n\nDo you need to book your ticket first? Book here(Link: https://www.kenya-airways.com/en-ke/book-a-flight/ ) and you will get an upgrade request email after you get your ticket.\n\nUpgrade at the Airport\n\nWhen you reach the check-in counter at the airport, request for an upgrade opportunity to be considered, and you will be presented with the following options:\n\n[List level 1] - Guests who purchase last-minute upgrades at the counter or onboard will retain their original Economy Class baggage allowance.\n\n[List level 1] - Purchasing a buy-up which means paying a fare difference between Economy Class ticket Fare and the available Business Class Fare. Kindly note this is subject to availability.\n\n[List level 1] - Last Minute Upgrades entails upgrading at the check in counter by paying a preset upgrade amount. Kindly note this is subject to availability.\n\n[List level 1] - Scan the self-upgrade QR code at check in or Transfer desks to complete your upgrade. Kindly note this is subject to Availability.\n\n[List level 1] - Scan the QR code on the Inflight Entertainment Screen to complete your upgrade. Kindly note this is subject to Availability.",
            "score": 0.8479740198521751
          },
          {
            "rank": 4,
            "parent_chunk_id": "53e2c5f1af391099ee23e0bfd24fbbf7382609aab60c057f12517160a6d2937f",
            "document": "Baggage Allowance Information.docx",
            "section": null,
            "text": "Preceding paragraph:\nYou may bring hand luggage on board the cabin during your journey with Kenya Airways in addition to the standard checked-in baggage allowance you are permitted to carry:\n\nTable (Body/block 196):\n\nOpening row (context, not a declared header):\nRow 1: Column 1: CABIN | Column 2: FLIGHTS TO/FROM\n  EU, US & UK* | Column 3: ALL OTHER ROUTES* | Column 4: PERSONAL\n ACCESSORIES\nRow 2: Column 1: Business Class | Column 2: 2 piece\n \n (max L55xW25xH35cm each)\n +\n 1 Accessory\n \n (Total weight max 18kgs/39lbs) | Column 3: 2 piece\n \n (max L55xW25xH35cm each)\n +\n 1 Accessory\n \n (Total weight max 18kgs/39lbs) | Column 4: The items below, maximum dimensions\n L40xW15xH30cms\n \n [List level 1] - Handbag\n \n [List level 1] - Backpack\n \n [List level 1] - Briefcase\n \n [List level 1] - Camera\n \n [List level 1] - Laptop\n \n [List level 1] - 1 duty free shopping bag per passenger\nRow 3: Column 1: Economy Class | Column 2: 1 piece\n \n (max L55xW25xH35cm each)\n +\n 1 accessory\n \n (Total weight max 12kgs/26lbs) | Column 3: 1 piece\n \n (max L55xW25xH35cm each)\n +\n 1 accessory\n \n (Total weight max 10kgs/22lbs) | Column 4: The items below, maximum dimensions\n L40xW15xH30cms\n \n [List level 1] - Handbag\n \n [List level 1] - Backpack\n \n [List level 1] - Briefcase\n \n [List level 1] - Camera\n \n [List level 1] - Laptop\n \n [List level 1] - 1 duty free shopping bag per passenger\n\nFollowing paragraph:\nAll cabin baggage shall have an \"approved KQ cabin luggage\" label attached as conformance to cabin baggage standards.",
            "score": 0.8100042827692501
          },
          {
            "rank": 5,
            "parent_chunk_id": "31cad70282aceb8596b8e786a6db1ab5da7cae336d86a9cf6c147cf7cd32edc6",
            "document": "Flight upgrade.docx",
            "section": null,
            "text": "Upgrade Flight\n\nUpgrade Flight link: https://www.kenya-airways.com/en-ke/book-manage/manage-booking/upgrade-flight/\n\nUpgrade to Business Class:\n\nYou now have various options of upgrading to our award-winning business class on Kenya Airways. With an economy class ticket, upgrading to business class and enjoying award-winning amenities is easy.\n\nBid to Upgrade:\n\nHolding an economy class ticket? Our Bid to Upgrade Program allows you to quote an amount you would like to pay for the upgrade to Business Class and if your bid is the highest, you will travel in style in Africa’s leading Business Class.\n\nYou can place your bid offer online up to 7–10 hours before departure, depending on your point of departure. With a little luck, your bid will be accepted.\n\nHave you already made your booking?\n\nEnter your details above to see if you qualify to upgrade your ticket.\n\nBenefits of upgrading to Business Class\n\n[List level 1] - Fly in Africa’s leading Business Class airline.\n\n[List level 1] - Speed through Jomo Kenyatta International Airport, Nairobi on the Sky Priority Lane through check-in, security and boarding.\n\n[List level 1] - A business class seat is guaranteed, with complimentary lounge access available at stations that offer lounge facilities, but there is no business class baggage allowance.\n\n[List level 1] - Enjoy the nouvelle cuisine onboard with a wide array of fine wines.\n\n[List level 1] - More than 100 movies, documentaries, and radio shows on a 15 inch screen for your in-flight entertainment.\n\n[List level 1] - A wide selection of newspapers and international magazines.",
            "score": 0.8466380427480066
          }
        ],
        "complete_supplied_evidence": [
          {
            "citation_id": "S1",
            "parent_chunk_id": "76643c828fc6fb4b87d43f454813fb09c8bea2b26343d64aeed622d8f3e85391",
            "text": "same amount. Otherwise, we will refund the amount.\n\nWhat happens if an Offer was cancelled by mistake?\n\nUp to 13 hours before departure you may cancel, correct your offer or re-offer.\n\nIs the time of making the Offer decisive for its ranking?\n\nNo.\n\nYou are travelling as a couple or family?\n\nUpgrade to business class considers all passengers within a joint booking.\n\nYou are travelling with a colleague who does not want to Upgrade to Business Class?\n\nAs long as you are not registered under one and the same booking number, you may submit your individual offer.\n\nWhat are the benefits of the KQ Upgrade to Business Class?\n\nYou receive an upgrade at an exceptional price and benefit from all amenities of the KQ Business Class, such as:\n\n[List level 1] - Award-winning Business Class Service and delicious catering\n\n[List level 1] - Access to our worldwide Business Lounges** including meals and drinks\n\n[List level 1] - Check-in at the Business Class counter and fast lane service**\n\n[List level 1] - NOTE: Business class passengers do not have miles accrual as a benefit\n\nCan Miles & More members redeem award miles for Upgrades?\n\nNo.\n\nWill the KQ Upgrade to Business Class change the conditions of your ticket?\n\nNo. The same rules apply as the original fare purchased, including Change Fees and Cancellation Penalties.\n\nIs it possible for one to modify Multicity bookings online?\n\nNo, It is not possible for any changes to be made on multi-city bookings.\n\nCan one make changes online to bookings that have been affected by schedule change?\n\nNo, one has to call our Contact center for Assistance.",
            "retrieval_rank": 1,
            "score": 0.8482578050412911
          },
          {
            "citation_id": "S2",
            "parent_chunk_id": "0112dbfe8e254d64f8ee4da022d1775c1c855fa2884cefbbdd9422dac8a3cd4c",
            "text": "onboard with a wide array of fine wines.\n\n[List level 1] - More than 100 movies, documentaries, and radio shows on a 15 inch screen for your in-flight entertainment.\n\n[List level 1] - A wide selection of newspapers and international magazines.\n\nNOTE: Tickets upgraded to Business class on the basis of a last minute airport upgrade, bid-upgrade, QR Code or on a complimentary basis accrue points on the basis of the original ticket purchased.\n\nDo you need to book your ticket first? Book here(Link: https://www.kenya-airways.com/en-ke/book-a-flight/ ) and you will get an upgrade request email after you get your ticket.\n\nUpgrade at the Airport\n\nWhen you reach the check-in counter at the airport, request for an upgrade opportunity to be considered, and you will be presented with the following options:\n\n[List level 1] - Guests who purchase last-minute upgrades at the counter or onboard will retain their original Economy Class baggage allowance.\n\n[List level 1] - Purchasing a buy-up which means paying a fare difference between Economy Class ticket Fare and the available Business Class Fare. Kindly note this is subject to availability.\n\n[List level 1] - Last Minute Upgrades entails upgrading at the check in counter by paying a preset upgrade amount. Kindly note this is subject to availability.\n\n[List level 1] - Scan the self-upgrade QR code at check in or Transfer desks to complete your upgrade. Kindly note this is subject to Availability.\n\n[List level 1] - Scan the QR code on the Inflight Entertainment Screen to complete your upgrade. Kindly note this is subject to Availability.",
            "retrieval_rank": 3,
            "score": 0.8479740198521751
          },
          {
            "citation_id": "S2",
            "parent_chunk_id": "31cad70282aceb8596b8e786a6db1ab5da7cae336d86a9cf6c147cf7cd32edc6",
            "text": "Upgrade Flight\n\nUpgrade Flight link: https://www.kenya-airways.com/en-ke/book-manage/manage-booking/upgrade-flight/\n\nUpgrade to Business Class:\n\nYou now have various options of upgrading to our award-winning business class on Kenya Airways. With an economy class ticket, upgrading to business class and enjoying award-winning amenities is easy.\n\nBid to Upgrade:\n\nHolding an economy class ticket? Our Bid to Upgrade Program allows you to quote an amount you would like to pay for the upgrade to Business Class and if your bid is the highest, you will travel in style in Africa’s leading Business Class.\n\nYou can place your bid offer online up to 7–10 hours before departure, depending on your point of departure. With a little luck, your bid will be accepted.\n\nHave you already made your booking?\n\nEnter your details above to see if you qualify to upgrade your ticket.\n\nBenefits of upgrading to Business Class\n\n[List level 1] - Fly in Africa’s leading Business Class airline.\n\n[List level 1] - Speed through Jomo Kenyatta International Airport, Nairobi on the Sky Priority Lane through check-in, security and boarding.\n\n[List level 1] - A business class seat is guaranteed, with complimentary lounge access available at stations that offer lounge facilities, but there is no business class baggage allowance.\n\n[List level 1] - Enjoy the nouvelle cuisine onboard with a wide array of fine wines.\n\n[List level 1] - More than 100 movies, documentaries, and radio shows on a 15 inch screen for your in-flight entertainment.\n\n[List level 1] - A wide selection of newspapers and international magazines.",
            "retrieval_rank": 5,
            "score": 0.8466380427480066
          }
        ],
        "rendered_context": "[S1]\nsame amount. Otherwise, we will refund the amount.\n\nWhat happens if an Offer was cancelled by mistake?\n\nUp to 13 hours before departure you may cancel, correct your offer or re-offer.\n\nIs the time of making the Offer decisive for its ranking?\n\nNo.\n\nYou are travelling as a couple or family?\n\nUpgrade to business class considers all passengers within a joint booking.\n\nYou are travelling with a colleague who does not want to Upgrade to Business Class?\n\nAs long as you are not registered under one and the same booking number, you may submit your individual offer.\n\nWhat are the benefits of the KQ Upgrade to Business Class?\n\nYou receive an upgrade at an exceptional price and benefit from all amenities of the KQ Business Class, such as:\n\n[List level 1] - Award-winning Business Class Service and delicious catering\n\n[List level 1] - Access to our worldwide Business Lounges** including meals and drinks\n\n[List level 1] - Check-in at the Business Class counter and fast lane service**\n\n[List level 1] - NOTE: Business class passengers do not have miles accrual as a benefit\n\nCan Miles & More members redeem award miles for Upgrades?\n\nNo.\n\nWill the KQ Upgrade to Business Class change the conditions of your ticket?\n\nNo. The same rules apply as the original fare purchased, including Change Fees and Cancellation Penalties.\n\nIs it possible for one to modify Multicity bookings online?\n\nNo, It is not possible for any changes to be made on multi-city bookings.\n\nCan one make changes online to bookings that have been affected by schedule change?\n\nNo, one has to call our Contact center for Assistance.\n\n[S2]\nonboard with a wide array of fine wines.\n\n[List level 1] - More than 100 movies, documentaries, and radio shows on a 15 inch screen for your in-flight entertainment.\n\n[List level 1] - A wide selection of newspapers and international magazines.\n\nNOTE: Tickets upgraded to Business class on the basis of a last minute airport upgrade, bid-upgrade, QR Code or on a complimentary basis accrue points on the basis of the original ticket purchased.\n\nDo you need to book your ticket first? Book here(Link: https://www.kenya-airways.com/en-ke/book-a-flight/ ) and you will get an upgrade request email after you get your ticket.\n\nUpgrade at the Airport\n\nWhen you reach the check-in counter at the airport, request for an upgrade opportunity to be considered, and you will be presented with the following options:\n\n[List level 1] - Guests who purchase last-minute upgrades at the counter or onboard will retain their original Economy Class baggage allowance.\n\n[List level 1] - Purchasing a buy-up which means paying a fare difference between Economy Class ticket Fare and the available Business Class Fare. Kindly note this is subject to availability.\n\n[List level 1] - Last Minute Upgrades entails upgrading at the check in counter by paying a preset upgrade amount. Kindly note this is subject to availability.\n\n[List level 1] - Scan the self-upgrade QR code at check in or Transfer desks to complete your upgrade. Kindly note this is subject to Availability.\n\n[List level 1] - Scan the QR code on the Inflight Entertainment Screen to complete your upgrade. Kindly note this is subject to Availability.\n\n[S2]\nUpgrade Flight\n\nUpgrade Flight link: https://www.kenya-airways.com/en-ke/book-manage/manage-booking/upgrade-flight/\n\nUpgrade to Business Class:\n\nYou now have various options of upgrading to our award-winning business class on Kenya Airways. With an economy class ticket, upgrading to business class and enjoying award-winning amenities is easy.\n\nBid to Upgrade:\n\nHolding an economy class ticket? Our Bid to Upgrade Program allows you to quote an amount you would like to pay for the upgrade to Business Class and if your bid is the highest, you will travel in style in Africa’s leading Business Class.\n\nYou can place your bid offer online up to 7–10 hours before departure, depending on your point of departure. With a little luck, your bid will be accepted.\n\nHave you already made your booking?\n\nEnter your details above to see if you qualify to upgrade your ticket.\n\nBenefits of upgrading to Business Class\n\n[List level 1] - Fly in Africa’s leading Business Class airline.\n\n[List level 1] - Speed through Jomo Kenyatta International Airport, Nairobi on the Sky Priority Lane through check-in, security and boarding.\n\n[List level 1] - A business class seat is guaranteed, with complimentary lounge access available at stations that offer lounge facilities, but there is no business class baggage allowance.\n\n[List level 1] - Enjoy the nouvelle cuisine onboard with a wide array of fine wines.\n\n[List level 1] - More than 100 movies, documentaries, and radio shows on a 15 inch screen for your in-flight entertainment.\n\n[List level 1] - A wide selection of newspapers and international magazines.",
        "decision": "context_available",
